diff --git a/prototypes/m7-gfx2/README.md b/prototypes/m7-gfx2/README.md
index 0d6a148..511d0c1 100644
--- a/prototypes/m7-gfx2/README.md
+++ b/prototypes/m7-gfx2/README.md
@@ -332,3 +332,38 @@ front-low and rear stills are brighter (mean luma +3.9 to +6.8 of 255). The comm
 chars, env, kit and render2 (`reports/captures/`) show those stages' frames from before polish1. The benchmark scenes
 need no new bake or asset: the scenes note in the Victus section still lists what a package must carry. On this tree,
 `scripts/capture-scenes.sh` renders 47 of 47 stills byte-identical to polish1's canonical set.
+
+## Visual critic iteration 2 (stage polish2)
+
+The thirteen ranked issues of the visual critic's second pass over the benchmark scenes, worked most visible first:
+hair through closed helmets, a cloud layer, the aftermath's disarmed prisoners and fallen (with fires and settled
+bodies), the river's banks, golden-hour ground cover, the close crowd's shading, the battle's marks on the ground,
+mid-distance faces, the avatar in a benchmark scene and an interactive capture sequence per scene. Presentation only
+(DR42): nothing reads back into the simulation and the battle trace is read-only. What changed, before/after per issue,
+llvmpipe costs, tests and what still looks placeholder: `reports/polish2.md`; provenance: `assets/PROVENANCE.md` §3.15
+(no new external asset).
+
+New render switches (`--set`). Gamut compression is on by default and so changes every G2 frame whose tone-mapped
+colour leaves the gamut; the cloud layer is drawn only where a scene sets a cover (the benchmark scenes set 0.30):
+
+| Switch | Meaning | Default; benchmark scenes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `gamut=<0..1>` | luminance-preserving compression of out-of-gamut chroma after the tone curve (knee 0.78, limit 0.88) | 1 |
+| `clouds=0\|1` | the cloud layer (sky and shadows) | on, but drawn only with a cover |
+| `cloudcover=<0..1>` | share of the sky under heaped cloud with the sun high | 0; 0.30 |
+| `cloudstreaks=<0..1>` | share under high streaks with the sun low (golden hour, dusk) | 0.42 |
+| `cloudshadow=<0..1>` | how much of the sun a thick cloud takes off the ground | 0.82 |
+| `cloudoffset=<x>:<z>` | the layer's offset (m): the scene's frozen wind; benchmark scenes pick the first of a fixed sequence that leaves their shot subjects in sun | 0:0; per scene |
+
+Defaults that reach every G2 frame, not only the benchmark scenes: gamut compression; the capped transmission chroma of
+grass cards and leaves and the per-tuft hue of the ground cover; the river-bank splat pass and the darker temperate rock
+of the env terrains; the crowd's duller iron, muted dyes and dimmed eye whites; the hero eyes' catchlight fading with
+distance; soft smoke particles wherever the G-buffer-lite is on. Review aid: `G2_REVIEW_CAM="ex,ey,ez,tx,ty,tz[,fovY]"`
+renders every picked shot of `--capture` from that camera (off by default; the canonical captures do not use it).
+
+```
+scripts/capture-scenes.sh OUT_DIR            # the canonical stills, plus the avatar's era triptych and a 12-frame
+                                             # interactive sequence per benchmark scene (groups avatar, motion)
+scripts/review-sheets-polish2.py BEFORE_DIR AFTER_DIR SHEETS_DIR REVIEW_DIR
+scripts/measure-polish2.py BEFORE_DIR AFTER_DIR
+```
